, so I don’t accidentally create unnecessary files or miss anything important. Following these guidelines will help keep everything organized and running smoothly. I want to make sure I'm getting this right!\"}]}"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_hyrvWbwBD5UIdTP0DVOZnrgo|fc_0f4b6da1e457fee30169baf758912c8191b2747d841111dae7","name":"read","arguments":{"file_path":"/home/lfant/.openclaw/workspace/HEARTBEAT.md"},"partialJson":"{\"file_path\":\"/home/lfant/.openclaw/workspace/HEARTBEAT.md\"}"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_cIsGDEs8dP91cYntM0QdInp9|fc_0f4b6da1e457fee30169baf75891388191879c59d126b4da7d","name":"read","arguments":{"file_path":"/home/lfant/.openclaw/workspace/SESSION-STATE.md"},"partialJson":"{\"file_path\":\"/home/lfant/.openclaw/workspace/SESSION-STATE.md\"}"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_mYRkkFEkQeYWxJUTFaOxtlI4|fc_0f4b6da1e457fee30169baf75891408191b45df693b4b831c6","name":"read","arguments":{"file_path":"/home/lfant/.openclaw/workspace/memory/working-buffer.md"},"partialJson":"{\"file_path\":\"/home/lfant/.openclaw/workspace/memory/working-buffer.md\"}"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_jdetzugNKVTm8rc5SSner77y|fc_0f4b6da1e457fee30169baf75891448191ae48fb887a47498e","name":"read","arguments":{"file_path":"/home/lfant/.openclaw/workspace/memory/heartbeat-state.json"},"partialJson":"{\"file_path\":\"/home/lfant/.openclaw/workspace/memory/heartbeat-state.json\"}"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_cc7GAh995wtiHD5j7Cak1w4v|fc_0f4b6da1e457fee30169baf758914c8191a24119bd0136cde0","name":"read","arguments":{"file_path":"/home/lfant/.openclaw/workspace/memory/2026-03-19.md"},"partialJson":"{\"file_path\":\"/home/lfant/.openclaw/workspace/memory/2026-03-19.md\"}"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_4pr16xGD0FH64us7STVoZDPh|fc_0f4b6da1e457fee30169baf75891508191b9f8b2edf3ef3902","name":"read","arguments":{"file_path":"~/.openclaw/cron/jobs.json"},"partialJson":"{\"file_path\":\"~/.openclaw/cron/jobs.json\"}"}],"api":"openai-codex-responses","provider":"openai-codex","model":"gpt-5.4","usage":{"input":1173,"output":220,"cacheRead":21504,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":22897,"cost":{"input":0.0029325,"output":0.0033,"cacheRead":0.005376,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.0116085}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1773860690811}}
{"type":"message","id":"99eae236","parentId":"b1f9b8f1","timestamp":"2026-03-18T19:04:55.665Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_hyrvWbwBD5UIdTP0DVOZnrgo|fc_0f4b6da1e457fee30169baf758912c8191b2747d841111dae7","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"# HEARTBEAT.md\n\n## Sam heartbeat routine\n\nUse this file only for **isolated agentTurn** heartbeat jobs.\nThis file is not the general chat heartbeat rule. It is only for isolated cron/agentTurn heartbeat jobs, so the terminal response is `NO_REPLY`, not `HEARTBEAT_OK`.\nThis job must stay **small, deterministic, and quiet**.\n\n### Scope\nOnly read these files unless one is missing and must be created:\n- `SESSION-STATE.md`\n- `memory/working-buffer.md`\n- `memory/heartbeat-state.json`\n- today's `memory/YYYY-MM-DD.md`\n- `~/.openclaw/cron/jobs.json`\n\n### Meaningful finding\nTreat a finding as meaningful only when one of these is true:\n- a cron job newly entered a non-ok state\n- a cron job remains in a non-ok state\n- a cron job has `consecutiveErrors > 0`\n- `SESSION-STATE.md` contains an explicit blocker, risk, or open follow-up\n- the current heartbeat status materially differs from the last recorded state\n\nIf none of the above changed, update `memory/heartbeat-state.json` only.\n\n### State file format\nUse ISO8601 timestamps.\nStore `findings` as an array of short strings.\nKeep entries concise, operational, and stable across repeated runs.\n\n### Duplicate control\nDo not append the same finding to today's daily memory more than once unless the state materially changed.\nIf a cron error persists with no status change, keep the finding in `memory/heartbeat-state.json` but avoid repeating the same daily-memory bullet.\n\n### Do on each heartbeat\n1. Ensure these files exist:\n   - `SESSION-STATE.md`\n   - `memory/working-buffer.md`\n   - `memory/heartbeat-state.json`\n   - today's daily memory file\n2. Check only these conditions:\n   - any cron job with `lastStatus != ok`\n   - any cron job with `consecutiveErrors > 0`\n   - any explicit blocker/risk/follow-up already listed in `SESSION-STATE.md`\n3. Update `memory/heartbeat-state.json` with:\n   - `lastRunAt`\n   - `lastChecks.sessionState`\n   - `lastChecks.dailyMemory`\n   - `lastChecks.cron`\n   - `findings`\n4. If there is a meaningful finding:\n   - append one short operational bullet to today's daily memory file only if it is new or materially changed\n   - update `SESSION-STATE.md` only if priorities, blockers, or active follow-ups actually changed\n   - keep the finding concise and operational\n5. If nothing meaningful changed:\n   - update `memory/heartbeat-state.json` only\n6. Always finish with `NO_REPLY`\n\n### Guardrails\n- No proactive messages from this job\n- No external actions\n- No large rewrites\n- No secrets, tokens, passwords, cookies, or raw PII in any memory file\n- File memory remains the auditable source of truth\n- `claude-mem` remains semantic recall, not the policy source of truth\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1773860695663}}
{"type":"message","id":"9fa6ee22","parentId":"99eae236","timestamp":"2026-03-18T19:04:55.667Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_cIsGDEs8dP91cYntM0QdInp9|fc_0f4b6da1e457fee30169baf75891388191879c59d126b4da7d","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"# SESSION-STATE.md\n\n**Updated:** 2026-03-16T15:26:00+09:00\n**Status:** active\n\n## Current focus\n- Memory baseline: `claude-mem` for semantic recall, file memory as auditable source of truth, proactive heartbeat for low-noise continuity.\n- Current task: keep local session-state aligned with current cron health and active priorities.\n\n## Active tasks\n- [x] Validate heartbeat state-file update path (manual verification completed)\n- [x] Reconfirm `github-repo-daily-briefing` cron health after the 2026-03-11 09:00 KST failure\n- [x] Investigate and resolve workspace-heartbeat job timeout (resolved 2026-03-16T15:26)\n- [x] Confirm `workspace-heartbeat` timeout condition is cleared (confirmed at 12:00 KST)\n- [x] Refresh stale follow-up items in local state files when cron health changes\n\n## Decisions\n- `claude-mem` remains the primary semantic memory layer\n- `MEMORY.md` and `memory/YYYY-MM-DD.md` remain the durable file-memory system of record\n- Proactive automation should be quiet by default and only escalate meaningful findings\n\n## Risks / watch items\n- The proactive loop was previously only partially implemented\n- Avoid storing secrets, tokens, cookies, or raw PII in any memory layer\n- Prevent drift between semantic memory and file memory by treating file memory as policy/audit SoT\n\n## Next actions\n- Keep heartbeat quiet-by-default while tracking cron failures or state drift in local files\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1773860695665}}
{"type":"message","id":"1410a3dd","parentId":"9fa6ee22","timestamp":"2026-03-18T19:04:55.668Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_mYRkkFEkQeYWxJUTFaOxtlI4|fc_0f4b6da1e457fee30169baf75891408191b45df693b4b831c6","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"# Working Buffer (Danger Zone Log)\n\n**Status:** INACTIVE\n**Started:** 2026-03-09T22:38:04+09:00\n**Activation Rule:** Start appending every exchange only when session context exceeds 60% or compaction risk is detected.\n\n---\n\n## Notes\n- Keep this file empty during normal operation.\n- When activated, append both the human message and a 1-2 sentence agent summary for each exchange.\n- After compaction/recovery, extract durable facts into `SESSION-STATE.md` or daily memory and then reset this file.\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1773860695666}}
